  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Ceric ammonium nitrate and CHCl<sub>3</sub>/alc. KOH are used for the identification of functional groups present in Alcohol and amine&nbsp;respectively.&nbsp;</p><p>Ceric ammonium nitrate for alcohol and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>KOH</mi></math>&nbsp;is carbyl amine test for primary amines.</p><p>Alcohol give positive test with ceric ammonium nitrate and primary amines gives carbyl amine test with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>KOH</mi></math>.</p>",
